<div class="guide-styles" data-zaf-dynamic="article" id="guide-body" lang="en">Welcome to Wowhead's Pre-Raid Best in Slot Gear list for Assassination Rogue DPS in Cataclysm Classic Phase 1. This guide will list the recommended gear for your class and role, containing gear sourced from dungeons, professions, Bind on Equip drops, reputations, justice points, and valor points.<h2 class="heading-size-2" id="best-in-slot">
<span class="c4">Best in Slot Gear for Assassination Rogue DPS in Pre-Patch</span></h2>An Assassination Rogue's first priority is meeting the Spell Hit Cap of 17%. This is made easier by flexing points in <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/spell=13843/precision">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/ability_marksmanship.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Precision</span></a>, reforging items to hit, and utilizing hit gems if necessary. After reaching the Spell Hit Cap, you will then look to stack as much Haste and Mastery as possible.<br/>
<br/>With the introduction of the reforging system, we will be able to take 40% of an unwanted or lesser valued stat and switch it over to a secondary stat that is not already present on the piece. As a  general rule, you'll aim to get your 17% spell cap and then make sure every piece has haste and mastery on it ideally by reforging off crit and expertise.<ol>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">Hit Rating - As mentioned, you will need to reach your hit cap of 17% (11% after 3/<wbr/>3 <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/spell=13843/precision">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/ability_marksmanship.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Precision</span></a>). We'll be targeting hit oriented pieces as well as reforging most of our crit/<wbr/>expertise to hit to meet this goal.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">Agility - Agility is the primary base stat for rogues, and is always good to get more of. We passively get 5% more of this stat in Cataclysm thanks to <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/spell=86531/leather-specialization">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_chest_leather_03.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Leather Specialization</span></a>. Agility gives 2 attack power per point and a little bit of critical strike chance for your attacks.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">Mastery - Mastery is an all new stat introduced in Cataclysm that has a unique effect based on whatever specialization you are playing. For Assassination, the mastery is <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/spell=76803/potent-poisons">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/trade_brewpoison.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Potent Poisons</span></a>. This increases our poison damage by 28% and increases  by 3.5% for every point of Mastery.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">Haste - This stat directly increases our energy regeneration in Cataclysm which is a big change for both the <a class="icontiny c4" data-entity="class" data-game="wow" data-type="class" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/class=4/rogue">
<img alt="Rogue" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/class_rogue.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Rogue</span></a> and <a class="icontiny c11" data-entity="class" data-game="wow" data-type="class" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/class=11/druid">
<img alt="Druid" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/class_druid.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Druid</span></a>. Haste is a very valuable stat for Assassination because it also increases our attack speed which in turn increases our poison applications.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">Expertise Rating - Expertise reduces the chance for our attacks to be dodged or parried. Assassination ignore expertise entirely as we are no longer as punished as we were for not being capped in Wrath. With the talent rework, rogues only lose 5 energy when missing abilities and considering we are not generally a GCD capped spec, is of no concern to us. We favor trading off expertise for more damaging stats.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">Critical Strike - This has the same effect it has always had in that it increases our critical strike chance doubling the amount of damage done when we do crit. Crit is an overall underwhelming stat for Rogues of all varieties in Cataclysm, with Assassination being no exception.</div></li></ol>
